  "prefLabel": "Abfd 302.02 2010 ADA Standards for Accessible Design",
  "priorExpiration": "2000-06-29",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Abfd 302.02 “2010 ADA Standards for Accessible Design” means the standards which the Department of Justice published in the Federal Register on September 15, 2010. These standards set minimum requirements, both scoping and technical, for newly designed and constructed or altered facilities to be readily accessible and usable by individuals with disabilities.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Abfd 100) #5720, eff 1-1-94, EXPIRED: 1-1-00\n\nNew. #7211, INTERIM, eff 3-1-00, EXPIRED: 6-29-00\n\nNew. #7347, eff 8-19-00; ss by #8011, eff 12-19-03; ss by #9234, eff 8-23-08; ss by #10248, eff 12-22-12; ss by #13674, eff 6-23-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/abfd100-300.html"
